WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:03.052
Line 3 is moving to hall B.

2
00:00:03.744 --> 00:00:08.249
The materials are right and so is the plan, but the project still gets stuck.

3
00:00:09.311 --> 00:00:10.716
Then it is about people.

4
00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:13.416
There are five stations for that.

5
00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:17.490
At each station you see what it is for, what you use,

6
00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:19.265
and what goes wrong without it.

7
00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:23.035
The first station is for when you are stuck.

8
00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:27.071
Line 3 stands still, and nobody knows why.

9
00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:29.770
Which of the four kinds of stuck is it?

10
00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:34.526
You find the facts with triangulation and a decision log.

11
00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.865
Without a diagnosis you push harder at the wrong problem.

12
00:00:40.151 --> 00:00:42.380
The second station is Leading people.

13
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:46.741
The buyer and the team lead do not report to you, but you need their help.

14
00:00:47.764 --> 00:00:50.597
You often use SBI and active listening.

15
00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:55.311
Without your own influence you keep borrowing power from the sponsor,

16
00:00:55.543 --> 00:00:56.541
and it wears out.

17
00:00:57.917 --> 00:01:01.365
The third station is Negotiating and holding your ground.

18
00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.994
The installer cannot make the date before the shutdown,

19
00:01:05.144 --> 00:01:06.642
and you need the power by then.

20
00:01:07.653 --> 00:01:10.126
You prepare with a BATNA and a fair standard.

21
00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:14.982
Without preparation you stand weak, and you dig in on positions.

22
00:01:16.286 --> 00:01:19.966
The fourth station is Leading projects outside your field.

23
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.145
One expert thinks the power cabinet is big enough, the other does not.

24
00:01:25.914 --> 00:01:29.246
You cannot judge the content, but you can structure the decision.

25
00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:32.995
You use a question set and a second opinion.

26
00:01:33.989 --> 00:01:36.125
Without this the loudest voice wins.

27
00:01:37.442 --> 00:01:40.124
The last station is Performance management.

28
00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:44.239
Line 3 is running, and you steer on a few numbers.

29
00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:48.232
You use a KPI tree and a performance board.

30
00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:52.261
Without this you get a wall of numbers nobody reads.

31
00:01:53.589 --> 00:01:55.261
This is the map of Projects.

32
00:01:55.969 --> 00:01:59.289
The five stations of the people side lie in a row.

33
00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.391
First When you are stuck, for diagnosis and restart.

34
00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:08.379
Then Leading people, for influence, feedback and coaching.

35
00:02:09.387 --> 00:02:13.718
Then Negotiating and holding your ground, from preparing to saying no.

36
00:02:14.727 --> 00:02:17.339
Then Leading projects outside your field,

37
00:02:17.444 --> 00:02:20.590
for asking questions and working with experts.

38
00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:26.028
Finally Performance management, for numbers, targets and the conversation.

39
00:02:27.138 --> 00:02:29.866
Each station is a module with four topics.

40
00:02:30.559 --> 00:02:31.871
Start where it hurts.
